{
  "frozen_descriptor": "A tall, gaunt humanoid figure standing approximately 1.9 meters, with a long, elongated silhouette. Head: a stark white ceramic plague-doctor mask with a curved, beak-like nose and dark, hollow eye sockets, fused seamlessly to the underlying flesh — no seam or gap visible along its edges. Body: a heavy, dark, hooded medieval plague-doctor robe in black, covering the entire frame from head to floor, with thick, pleated fabric obscuring any anatomical detail. Hands: bare, pale, gaunt, with long, slender fingers — the only exposed skin, visibly unnerving in its stillness. Limbs long and thin, moving with deliberate. slow, measured gestures. Carried item: a worn, dark leather medical bag, held at its side. The mask is not a removable accessory; it is visually integrated into the entity's head, as if grown into the bone and tissue.",
  "entity_sheet": "SCP-049 is the medieval plague doctor whose ceramic beak mask is fused permanently to its face — the single most recognizable visual trait. Its behavioral signature is the silent space it occupies and the hushed aftermath it leaves: after a fatal touch, the air stills, the body falls without a sound, and the entity calmly produces its leather bag and begins its surgical work, as if performing a routine procedure.",
  "story_logline": "A self-proclaimed doctor believes he is curing a plague only he can see — but every patient he touches dies instantly, and every corpse he operates on rises again, altered. The video asks whether SCP-049 is a healer, a killer, or something that no longer remembers the difference.",
